The champion only gives a top‑level bonus when it kills a pirate that is already at position 2. In many levels a pirate at position 1 (or 0) will become a position 2 next round and then require extra damage, yet the policy treats killing it the same as doing nothing. I add a second “any‑kill” priority (after the existing *kill‑pos‑2* check) so actions that eliminate the current front pirate – even if it is not at position 2 – are preferred before looking at deficit or future look‑ahead. This small tweak fixes cases where killing a position 1 pirate now prevents an unavoidable loss later.

